      "math_academy_id": "q-125574",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/841dfcfabb27fe93002cb05c8d84ad9da2e0a9f6b810476e7964651e515e757c.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the point $(8,-6)$ under the action of a dilation with center $O$ and scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "A dilation with center at the origin and a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(\\frac{1}{2}x,\\frac{1}{2}y).\n$$\n\nApplying this function to the point $(8,-6),$ we have\n\n$$\n(8,-6)↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-6))=(4,-3).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resulting point is $(4,-3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/53df2214415b81380c96af98b2d073e2a16480715386926603cd471eec66dec6.png)",
